KHẢO SÁT MEA — third-party assets in this film

Fonts (all SIL Open Font License 1.1, served locally as Vietnamese subsets
via google-webfonts-helper):
- Barlow Condensed (300, 500) — Jeremy Tribby. Reading numerals.
- IBM Plex Mono (500, used at 400/500) — IBM / Mike Abbink, Bold Monday.
  Instruments and coordinates.
- Noto Sans (500, 700) — Google / Noto project. Labels, title, end card.

Software:
- three.js (MIT, (c) 2010-2024 three.js authors) — WebGL point/surface
  rendering in the film page, via the library's node_modules.
- lemo-opuscar production library (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab) — the shared
  core tools used to render, check and master this film
  (core/render/video.mjs, events.mjs, readcheck.mjs, mux.sh). The library
  is a tool; no material from its demo films appears in this film.
- FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL, ffmpeg.org) — encoding and loudness mastering.

Everything else was made for this film:
- Point data: generated on this machine from Mea's real system inventory
  (method and sources in FACTS.md). No stock imagery, no external data.
- Sound: every sound is synthesized in mix.py (numpy) — no sample
  libraries, no recorded music, no voice.
